# Env names only — never values. Secrets travel vault -> render -> env,
# never through git.
#
# One block per plugin that exists in this repo. Later waves add their own;
# do not pre-declare names for plugins that are not here yet.

# ── notes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# notes-srv has NO users. NOTES_API_KEY is both the credential AND the
# top-level folder this profile may write under (key `claude` -> writes
# `claude` and `claude/...`, nothing else). Each profile needs its OWN key:
# a shared one means every agent writes into one folder as one identity.
# There is deliberately no NOTES_USER_ID — there is no user to identify.
# NOTES_URL=
# NOTES_API_KEY=

# ══ app-bridge plugin ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# fin3-bridge and vita3-bridge were two plugins until 2026-08-15; they are now
# one `app-bridge` plugin with two toolsets. Every variable below kept its
# name, so nothing in a profile .env had to move.
#
# <APP>_URL and <APP>_TOOL_KEY are now GUARDED: with either unset the bridge
# refuses by name and fires no request. It used to raise ValueError out of the
# tool handler instead, which is what made a port-less VITA3_URL read as a
# broken plugin rather than a typo.

# ── fin3 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FIN3_USER_ID is absent on purpose in the default `fin3` profile: without it
# every forwarded call fails the server-side identity check, so the default
# can act for nobody.
# FIN3_URL=
# FIN3_TOOL_KEY=
# FIN3_USER_ID=

# ── vita3 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITA3_URL=
# VITA3_TOOL_KEY=
# VITA3_USER_ID=

# ── recipes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# recipe-srv is a single-user LAN app with NO auth — no key, no user id.
# RECIPES_URL=

# ── home ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No block: the `home` plugin targeted home-srv-v2 (/api/v2, X-Home-Key) and
# was deleted on 2026-08-07 when the app moved to v3 (container `home3`). Its
# test and this block outlived it and were removed 2026-08-15. home-srv-v3 is
# OUR app, so when it comes back it comes back as a BRIDGE, and it declares
# its own names then — this file does not pre-declare for plugins that are
# not here.

# ── weather ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Open-Meteo is KEYLESS. There is no WEATHER_API_KEY; don't go looking.
# WEATHER_LAT=
# WEATHER_LON=

# ══ media plugin ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# radarr, sonarr, lidarr, plex, nzb and tmdb were six plugins until
# 2026-08-15; they are now one `media` plugin with six toolsets. Every
# variable below kept its name, so nothing in a profile .env had to move.

# ── radarr ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Third-party, single-tenant: one shared library, so no user id.
# RADARR_URL=
# RADARR_API_KEY=

# ── sonarr / lidarr ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SONARR_URL=
# SONARR_API_KEY=
# LIDARR_URL=
# LIDARR_API_KEY=

# ── plex ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PLEX_URL=
# PLEX_TOKEN=

# ── tmdb ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Key travels as a QUERY PARAM, so it is redacted from error messages.
# TMDB_API_KEY=

# ── nzb ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NZB_URL needs its TRAILING SLASH. The password is in the URL path, so the
# URL is redacted from every error message.
# NZB_URL=
# NZB_USER=
# NZB_PASSWORD=

# ── minimax ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=

# ── tickets / cal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The KEY is the identity — looked up in the shared identity table, and
# username and apiKey are the same value by convention. Each profile gets its
# OWN key; no user id is sent at all. Both apps gained key auth on 2026-08-05
# (tickets-srv 96df76c, cal-srv cd38b84); before that they trusted a bare
# X-User-Id header and neither plugin could safely exist.
# TICKETS_URL=
# TICKETS_API_KEY=
# CAL_URL=
# CAL_API_KEY=
